    "description": "The Self-Consciousness Scale - Revised (SCS-R) is a 21-item self-report questionnaire measuring individual differences in the tendency to attend to oneself, covering public self-consciousness, private self-consciousness, and social anxiety. It is used in personality and social psychology research to examine how self-focused attention relates to behavior, affect, and interpersonal functioning.",
